    "model": "Ethanoic acid: moles = 1.0 × 50/1000 = 0.05 mol acid = 0.05 mol H⁺\nΔHn = −2.79 ÷ 0.05 = −55.8 kJ mol⁻¹\n\nSulphuric acid: moles = 0.05 mol acid = 0.1 mol H⁺ (0.1 mol H₂O formed)\nΔHn = −5.72 ÷ 0.1 = −57.2 kJ mol⁻¹ (per mole of H⁺ / H₂O)\n\nReason: sulphuric acid is a strong acid, fully ionised (present as ions), so no energy is needed to dissociate it. Ethanoic acid is a weak acid, mostly present as molecules, so some energy is needed to ionise it, which reduces the heat released.",
