    "marks": 12,
    "model": "Ka = [H⁺]² / (0.1 − [H⁺]) = 3.7 × 10⁻⁸\nThe acid is only slightly dissociated, so 0.1 − [H⁺] ≈ 0.1, giving [H⁺]² = 3.7 × 10⁻⁸ × 0.1 = 3.7 × 10⁻⁹\n[H⁺] = √(3.7 × 10⁻⁹) = 6 × 10⁻⁵ mol dm⁻³\nPercentage dissociation = (6 × 10⁻⁵ / 0.1) × 100 = 0.06 %",
