    "model": "Al₂O₃: amphoteric. CO: neutral. MgO: basic. CO₂: acidic.\n\nAl₂O₃ is amphoteric because it reacts with both acids and bases. CO is neutral—it is neither acidic nor basic as it does not react with aqueous NaOH or HCl. MgO is basic because magnesium is a highly electropositive metal in Group 2; its oxide is ionic and alkaline in water. CO₂ is acidic because carbon is a non-metal in Group 14; its oxide is covalent and forms a weak acid (H₂CO₃) in water, reacting with bases.",
