    "marks": 18,
    "model": "Oxidation numbers:\nMnO₄⁻: Mn = +7 → Mn²⁺: Mn = +2, so Mn is reduced (gains 5 e⁻).\nC₂O₄²⁻: C = +3 → CO₂: C = +4, so C is oxidised (each C loses 1 e⁻).\nOxidation half-equation: C₂O₄²⁻ → 2CO₂ + 2e⁻ (multiply by 5)\nReduction half-equation: MnO₄⁻ + 8H⁺ + 5e⁻ → Mn²⁺ + 4H₂O (multiply by 2)\nBalanced equation: 2MnO₄⁻ + 16H⁺ + 5C₂O₄²⁻ → 2Mn²⁺ + 10CO₂ + 8H₂O\n(halved: MnO₄⁻ + 8H⁺ + 2½C₂O₄²⁻ → Mn²⁺ + 5CO₂ + 4H₂O)",
