    "model": "When the second portion of potassium manganate(VII) is added, the decolorising time becomes shorter because Mn²⁺ ions are produced during the first reaction. Mn²⁺ ions catalyse the redox reaction between MnO₄⁻ and C₂O₄²⁻, increasing the reaction rate. The reaction is autocatalytic: Mn²⁺ ions lower the activation energy of the reaction, allowing the second portion of permanganate to react more rapidly with the remaining oxalate ions, so the purple colour fades more quickly.",
