    "model": "Sodium is stored under oil because it is highly reactive and would oxidise or react with moisture in air. When sodium reacts with water, the gas evolved is hydrogen. The reaction is: 2Na + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + H₂↑. The reaction is vigorous and exothermic, producing a bright yellow flame.",
