    "model": "A catalyst is a substance that increases the rate of a chemical reaction without being consumed in the reaction. It lowers the activation energy of the reaction by providing an alternative reaction pathway.\n\n(i) Ammonia production: activated iron oxide (Fe₂O₃)\n(ii) Nitric acid production: rhodium-platinum gauze (Rh/Pt)\n(iii) Sulphuric acid production: vanadium pentoxide (V₂O₅)\n\nBalanced equation for ammonia synthesis:\nN₂(g) + 3H₂(g) ⇌ 2NH₃(g) [catalysed by Fe₂O₃]\n\nAlternatively, for sulphuric acid production:\n2SO₂(g) + O₂(g) ⇌ 2SO₃(g) [catalysed by V₂O₅]",
