    "marks": 9,
    "model": "Across period 2 (Li to Ne), the atomic radius decreases.\nAccount: the nuclear charge (number of protons) increases across the period. The number of inner shells and the screening effect of the inner electrons stay constant. The stronger attraction of the nucleus pulls the outer electrons closer, so the radius decreases.",
