    "model": "Paper chromatography of a mixture of indicators\n\nDiagram:\n\n      ┌── lid ──┐\n      │  paper  │ ← chromatography paper (stationary phase)\n      │  ░ ░ ░  │ ← separated coloured spots\n      │    ░    │\n      │  ● spot │ ← spot of indicator mixture (origin), about 2 cm above bottom\n   ───┼─────────┼─── ← solvent level (eluent / mobile phase)\n      └─ tank ──┘\n\nMethod:\n1. Using a dropper (capillary tube), place a small spot of the indicator mixture on the chromatography paper about 2 cm above the bottom of the sheet.\n2. Place the paper in the tank (beaker) so that the bottom dips into the eluent (solvent, mobile phase) with the spot above the level of the solvent. Cover the tank with the lid.\n3. Elute: the solvent moves up the paper, carrying the components of the mixture up at different rates.\n4. Remove the paper when the solvent has risen near the top (when eluted).\n5. The mixture is separated into distinct coloured spots at different heights, one for each indicator.",
