    "marks": 6,
    "model": "Hydrogen sulfide is non-linear (bent or V-shaped).\nJustification: the S atom has two non-bonding (lone) pairs in its valence shell. That gives four electron pairs around S, which repel each other and push the two H atoms into a bent shape.",
    "model_source": "haiku",
