    "model": "All three products form from one common intermediate, the carbocation (or bromonium ion). It is attacked by different nucleophiles (Br⁻, Cl⁻ and H₂O).\nThe products containing Cl and OH groups show that the intermediate is ionic and that a negative ion or water molecule attacks it in a second step.\nThis fits a two-step ionic addition mechanism, not a concerted or free-radical process.",
