    "model": "The octane number of a fuel is a measure of its resistance to knocking (premature auto-ignition) in an engine.\nIt is compared with two reference fuels: iso-octane, rated 100, and heptane, rated 0.\nThe octane number is the percentage by volume of iso-octane in a mixture of iso-octane and heptane that has the same knocking behaviour as the fuel.",
