    "model": "pH is defined as the negative logarithm (to base 10) of the hydrogen ion concentration. pH = –log₁₀[H⁺] where [H⁺] is the concentration of hydrogen ions in moles per litre.",
    "model_source": "audited",
    "answerStatus": "kept",
