    "model": "Diagram (described): a tall fractionating column with trays or plates. It is hotter at the bottom and cooler at the top. Label the liquid air inlet near the bottom, the nitrogen outlet at the top and the liquid oxygen tap at the base.\nProcess: the liquid air is fed in and warms up as it rises through the column, so its components boil off at different temperatures.\nLiquid oxygen, which has the highest boiling point, collects at the base and is removed there. Gaseous nitrogen, which has the lowest boiling point (−196 °C), rises to the top and is drawn off.",
