    "model": "Moles of thiosulfate = 0.10 × 16.1 ÷ 1000 = 1.61 × 10⁻³ mol\nFrom 2S₂O₃²⁻ + I₂: moles of I₂ = 1.61 × 10⁻³ ÷ 2 = 8.05 × 10⁻⁴ mol\nFrom ClO⁻ + 2I⁻ + 2H⁺: 1 mol ClO⁻ gives 1 mol I₂, so moles of NaClO in 25.0 cm³ = 8.05 × 10⁻⁴ mol\nConcentration = 8.05 × 10⁻⁴ ÷ 0.0250 dm³ = 0.0322 mol L⁻¹ (0.032 mol L⁻¹)",
