    "model": "Same pH, so [H⁺] = 10⁻²·⁴⁵ = 3.55 × 10⁻³ mol l⁻¹.\nH₂SO₄ → 2H⁺ + SO₄²⁻, so one mole of sulfuric acid gives two moles of H⁺.\n[H₂SO₄] = [H⁺] ÷ 2 = 3.55 × 10⁻³ ÷ 2 = 1.77 × 10⁻³ mol l⁻¹ (about 1.75–1.77 × 10⁻³ mol l⁻¹).",
