    "label": "(b)(ii)",
    "marks": 15,
    "model": "Saturate the tank: pour a little solvent (eluent) into a covered tank and leave it so the air inside is saturated with solvent vapour.\nPrepare the plate: draw a pencil line about 1 to 2 cm from the bottom of a chromatography paper or TLC plate.\nApply the sample: using a capillary tube, put a small spot of the mixture (e.g. ink) on the pencil line and allow it to dry.\nArrange with eluent: stand the plate upright in the tank so the bottom edge is just in the solvent, with the spot above the solvent level, then close the tank.\nElution: the solvent rises up the plate by capillary action and carries the components at different rates. Remove the plate before the solvent reaches the top and mark the solvent front.\nObserve separation: the mixture separates into separate coloured spots, which can be compared with known substances.",
