    "marks": 7,
    "model": "Intramolecular: forces between atoms in (within, inside) molecules. Intermolecular: forces between molecules. (i) Hydrogen smaller / has fewer (two) electrons; therefore weaker (less) intermolecular (van der Waals, dispersion, London, dipole-dipole) forces (attractions, interactions). (ii) Iodine pure covalent (non-polar); water a polar solvent; intermolecular (van der Waals, etc.) forces (attractions, interactions) between iodine and water very weak. (iii) Charge on rod attracts; opposite charge on polar (dipole of) water molecule",
    "model_source": "audited",
