    "model": "1. Chemical reactions involve only electrons (bonds are broken and formed) and leave the nucleus unchanged, so the elements remain the same. Nuclear reactions involve changes in the nucleus and can form new elements (transmutation).\n2. Chemical reactions conserve mass and involve small energy changes. In nuclear reactions some mass is converted into a very large amount of energy (E = mc²).",
