    "model": "Moles of NH₄OH = 7.0 g ÷ 35 g mol⁻¹ = 0.20 mol, so concentration = 0.20 mol L⁻¹\n[OH⁻] = √(Kb × c) = √(1.8 × 10⁻⁵ × 0.20) = 1.9 × 10⁻³ mol L⁻¹\npOH = −log(1.9 × 10⁻³) = 2.72\npH = 14.00 − 2.72 = 11.28 (≈ 11.3)",
