    "marks": 6,
    "model": "Yes, a limestone district would be expected to have hard water.\nReason: limestone is calcium carbonate. Rainwater containing dissolved carbon dioxide (carbonic acid, H₂CO₃) dissolves some of it, so the water contains calcium ions (Ca²⁺), which make it hard.",
