    "model": "Mass of phenylmethanol = 1.5 cm³ × 1.04 g cm⁻³ = 1.56 g.\nMoles of phenylmethanol = 1.56 g ÷ 108 g mol⁻¹ = 0.0144 mol.\nMoles of KMnO₄ = 3.16 g ÷ 158 g mol⁻¹ = 0.02 mol.\nFrom the equation, 3 mol phenylmethanol react with 4 mol KMnO₄, so 0.0144 mol needs 0.0144 × 4/3 = 0.0192 mol KMnO₄.\nThere is 0.02 mol KMnO₄, which is more than 0.0192 mol, so there is sufficient KMnO₄. The KMnO₄ is in excess and phenylmethanol is the limiting reagent.",
