    "model": "Diagram, in words: draw two or more water molecules, each as an O atom with two H atoms attached. Label the O atom δ⁻ and each H atom δ⁺, because O is much more electronegative than H, so each O–H bond is polar. Draw a hydrogen bond as a dotted line from the δ⁺ hydrogen of one water molecule to the δ⁻ oxygen of a neighbouring molecule, and label it 'hydrogen bond'.\nExplanation: the δ⁺ hydrogen of one molecule is attracted to the lone pair on the δ⁻ oxygen of another molecule. This is a strong intermolecular attraction, which needs a lot of energy to overcome, so the boiling point of water is high.",
